-- title:
--   A graded piece of LieΦ lies in kervarpī
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\iota \colon \mathbb{Z}_{p^2} = W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism, and write $j$ for the composite of $\iota$ with the quotient map $W(k) \to W(k)/pW(k)$, where $pW(k)$ denotes the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B = W(k)/pW(k)$, that is, a commutative two-dimensional formal group law over $B$ together with an action $a \mapsto \Phi.\mathrm{act}\,a$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ by endomorphisms of the law (multiplicative and additive in $a$, sending $1$ to the identity) and a further endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi \circ \varpi = \mathrm{act}\,p$ and $\varpi \circ \mathrm{act}\,a = \mathrm{act}(\sigma a) \circ \varpi$ for the Witt-vector Frobenius $\sigma$. Assume $\Phi$ is special for $j$: the submodules $(\operatorname{Lie}\Phi)_0 = \bigcap_a \ker(\mathrm{lieAct}\,a - j(a)\,\mathrm{id})$ and $(\operatorname{Lie}\Phi)_1 = \bigcap_a \ker(\mathrm{lieAct}\,a - j(\sigma a)\,\mathrm{id})$ of $\operatorname{Lie}\Phi$ are complementary and each is an invertible $B$-module; assume also that $\Phi$ has height $4$, i.e. the predicate `HasKernelOfDegree` holds for the series $\mathrm{act}\,p$ with degree $p^4$. Then at least one of $(\operatorname{Lie}\Phi)_0$ and $(\operatorname{Lie}\Phi)_1$ is contained in the kernel of `Φ.lieVarpi`, the $B$-linear endomorphism of $\operatorname{Lie}\Phi$ given by multiplication by the matrix of linear coefficients of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the statement that for a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module one of the two eigen-pieces of the Lie algebra is critical, in the sense that the linear part of $\varpi$ annihilates it; here it is recorded over the residue ring $W(k)/pW(k)$ of the Witt vectors of an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. It feeds the Čerednik–Drinfeld analysis of Drinfeld data and admissible covers, being used in the characterisation of rigidified special formal modules arising by base change from an admissible cover.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_lieZero_le_ker_lieVarpi_or_lieOne_le_ker_lieVarpi_of_isSpecial_wittVector_quotient.lean

